@page
@model AboutModel
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "About";
}

<h1>About RepoSummary</h1>

<div class="card">
    <p class="lead">
        RepoSummary helps developers translate real project work into confident,
        specific, interview-ready language — without exaggerating.
    </p>
    <p>
        Most AI résumé tools invent impressive-sounding claims. RepoSummary does the
        opposite: it starts from <strong>evidence</strong>. It reads a public GitHub
        repository, surfaces the facts — technologies, structure, commits, dependencies,
        and documentation — and only then helps you talk about that work.
    </p>
    <p>
        <a class="btn btn-primary" asp-page="/Index">Analyze a repository →</a>
    </p>
</div>

<div class="card">
    <h2>What it does</h2>
    <ol class="clean">
        <li><strong>Reads the repo.</strong> Enter a public repository (owner/repo or a URL). RepoSummary pulls metadata, the README, recent commits, languages, the full file tree, and parsed dependency manifests through GitHub's public API.</li>
        <li><strong>Extracts evidence.</strong> It detects technologies and versions, the architecture pattern, database/ORM, API surface, CI/CD workflows, security tooling, releases, and commit patterns — then rolls them into an A–F project maturity score.</li>
        <li><strong>Suggests how to talk about it.</strong> Rule-based résumé angles and interview talking points come free, each tied to what's actually in the repo.</li>
        <li><strong>Keeps a library.</strong> Analyses are saved locally so you can reopen them, see your skills add up across projects, compare two repos, and build a portfolio.</li>
    </ol>
</div>

<div class="card">
    <h2>AI writing <span class="tag-optional">optional</span></h2>
    <p>
        Add your own OpenAI (ChatGPT) or Anthropic (Claude) key in
        <a asp-page="/Settings" asp-route-returnUrl="/About">Settings</a> to generate
        résumé bullets, STAR interview stories, project summaries, cover letters, a
        LinkedIn "About", technical case studies, and README improvements — with
        streaming output and the option to tailor everything to a job description.
    </p>
    <p class="hint">
        The key stays encrypted on this machine and you pay your provider directly.
        Everything else — evidence, detected tech, maturity score, and rule-based
        angles — works with no key at all.
    </p>
</div>

<div class="card">
    <h2>The core rule</h2>
    <p>
        Every strong claim ties back to real repository evidence. If the app can't
        point to a commit, a file, a technology, or a piece of documentation, it doesn't
        make the claim — and the generated writing is instructed to do the same.
    </p>
</div>
